Bootstrap: docker-daemon
From: qedrank-lean:latest

# The QEDRank Lean environment as an Apptainer image, from the Docker image that
# `node qedrank/cli.js lean-env build --project <dir>` produced on a machine with Docker:
#
#   apptainer build qedrank-lean.sif lean-env/qedrank-lean.def
#
# `lean-env build --apptainer` does the same (or, without Apptainer on the build machine, writes
# a docker-archive tar and prints the `apptainer build ... docker-archive://...` command to run on
# the cluster). Docker's ENV (ELAN_HOME, PATH) is carried over, so `lake env` works under
# `apptainer exec --containall --cleanenv`, which is how QEDRank runs it. See lean-env/README.md.

%labels
    org.qedrank.lean-env 1

%help
    QEDRank Lean environment: /project is a built Lean project with its toolchain.
    QEDRank runs `lean` in it with the run folders bound at /work:
      node qedrank/cli.js run ... --backend apptainer --sif qedrank-lean.sif
